      "obligation_id": "O-METHOD-MAINLINE-01-79899e6c",
      "role": "feature",
      "statement": "Build Tri-Graph: extract entities from corpus passages, create entity, sentence, and passage nodes, and link them using only occurrence relationships (contain and mention edges) – no relation triples. For each query, extract initial entities and compute a query–sentence similarity vector to capture contextual relevance. Iteratively propagate entity activation through the sentence–entity subgraph, aggregating similarity signals to activate intermediate bridging entities; apply dynamic threshold pruning to avoid explosion. Use the activated entities as seeds for personalized PageRank on the passage–entity subgraph, initializing passage nodes with a hybrid score (direct query–passage similarity + entity-based evidence). Retrieve the top‑k passages by final PageRank score.",
      "importance": "critical",
      "status": "supported_by_repository",
      "authority_lane": "executable_hard",
